Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 14:58:10 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 17/17] Let Serato and Rekordbox data win, with
 [Library],HonorExternalMetadata

[AI-generated text: this description was written autonomously by an AI
agent (Claude). Review it before relying on it or submitting it.]

Mixxx reads a file's tags, Serato's grid and cues included, once: later
changes are only read back with file tag sync on, Serato data only with
Serato metadata export on too (both make Mixxx write into the files), and
then existing hot cues still stop Serato's cues from being imported.
Rekordbox grids are re-applied on every load from the Rekordbox view, but
not over a BPM lock, and hot cues deleted in Rekordbox stay.

With HonorExternalMetadata (off by default; no preferences UI) the other
library wins whenever its data changes, and Mixxx writes nothing:
- a file modified since its tags were last read is read again when its
  track is loaded, Serato data included;
- a re-read Serato grid replaces the track's even if the BPM is locked,
  and Serato's cues replace Mixxx's cues of the same types; cue types
  Serato has no word for (intro, outro, ...) stay;
- loaded from the Rekordbox view, a track takes Rekordbox's grid over a
  BPM lock, and loses hot cues Rekordbox no longer has.

Track::tryImportBeats() and importCueInfos() gain the flags for this,
off by default.

Tested on Windows: new tests for the re-read of a changed file with
only this setting on, and for the grid and cue imports with and
without their overrides, pass with the existing track, sync and Serato
tests. Not yet tried against a library Serato or Rekordbox changed.

[End of AI-generated text.]

